CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F308A1785442291
OL,3,CHow much rain would it take to end a
OL,4,Cdrought in the UK?
OL,6,FRainfall totals have been
OL,7,Fsignificantly below average through
OL,8,Fthe summer, leaving soils parched,
OL,9,Frivers running lower and increasing
OL,10,Fpressure on water supplies.
OL,12,FThe lack of rainfall has followed an
OL,13,Fextended spell of settled weather,
OL,14,Fwith high pressure dominating for much
OL,15,Fof late spring and summer. This has
OL,16,Flimited the opportunity for widespread
OL,17,Frain.
OL,19,FSome areas are now being moved into
OL,20,Fdrought status as water resources come
OL,21,Funder increasing pressure.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G4/9
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
