CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F308A1785442291
OL,3,CHow much rain would it take to end a
OL,4,Cdrought in the UK?
OL,6,FHeavy downpours can help temporarily,
OL,7,Fbut much of that water can run off
OL,8,Fquickly rather than soaking into dry
OL,9,Fground and replenishing water sources.
OL,11,FWhat is needed is a sustained period
OL,12,Fof above-average rainfall spread
OL,13,Facross many weeks, allowing soils to
OL,14,Frecover and rivers, reservoirs and
OL,15,Funderground water supplies to rebuild.
OL,17,FThe rainfall deficit built up over
OL,18,Fmonths cannot usually be reversed by
OL,19,Fone wet day or even one wet week,
OL,20,Fdrought recovery often takes much
OL,21,Flonger than drought development.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G6/9
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,309,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30807
SC,0007
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F308A1785442291
OL,3,CHow much rain would it take to end a
OL,4,Cdrought in the UK?
OL,6,FWould we be in a worse position
OL,7,Fwithout the wet winter - and what
OL,8,Fhappens next?
OL,10,FAlthough the current conditions are
OL,11,Fvery dry, the UK entered summer with a
OL,12,Fhelpful buffer thanks to a wetter
OL,13,Fwinter (and autumn).
OL,15,FThat rainfall helped recharge
OL,16,Fgroundwater and maintain river levels
OL,17,Fbefore the prolonged dry spell began.
OL,19,FWithout that earlier rainfall, water
OL,20,Fresources would likely be under even
OL,21,Fgreater pressure now.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G7/9
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
